  "problem": "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx={t}^{2}-2,\\,\\,\\,y=3-t,\\,-3\\le t\\le 3\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x={t}^{2}-2.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $2$ | $7$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=3-t.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $2$ | $7$ |\n| $y$ | $6$ | $5$ | $4$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/assets/6a66ca74691344866c4f754edf36acc2f5301a0eeecee6340a0a701ad99f5fd6.png)",
